+##
+# @x-fdisbull-arm-mouse-click:
+#
+# @token: Unused owner token of 1..128 bytes, shared with other input arms.
+# @button: Ordinary left, middle or right mouse button; no wheel/side/extra.
+# @hold-ms: Hold from the actual down callback, 1..1000 milliseconds.
+#
+# Passively arm one down/up pair on the valid stopped native clock profile.
+# Validate the button, hold and full signed nominal horizon, then prepare and
+# pin two separate one-event PS/2 batches before accepting the token.  The
+# down is due 2 ms after arm.  Its callback and sync establish the release
+# deadline hold-ms later; a late down never shortens the requested hold.
+#
+# Every edge preserves the existing epoch/profile, pending-stop, reached/equal
+# clock-budget and pinned-handler checks.  The first actual VM stop cancels
+# the undispatched suffix.  Completion does not itself stop the VM.  There
+# is no implicit run, movement, trailing timer, replay or cleanup release.
+#
+# Shares query/cancel, migration restriction and token history with other
+# input modes.  Successful arm clears press/typing/retrace descriptors;
+# another accepted arm clears click.  Refused arms preserve the old receipt
+# and do not consume the requested token.  External button state and pending
+# mouse accumulators are not neutralized.  Disabled, remote or full devices
+# can complete callbacks without emitting a packet or delivering guest input.
+#
+# Returns: Armed receipt with only the down deadline established.
+# Since: 10.0
+##
+{ 'command': 'x-fdisbull-arm-mouse-click',
+  'data': { 'token': 'str', 'button': 'InputButton', 'hold-ms': 'int' },
